slack.zip, upath.zip, stored-dd.zip and SHA256SUMS are mihailinl/AstraPlugins'
testdata/zip-cloaking/ files, byte for byte (PR #122: slack.zip and upath.zip at daa9f05,
stored-dd.zip at 62e8106; on its master since 7804f9a, and unchanged at 4976d60). Every reader of
an archive Astra installs refuses all three, and each pins them by the sha256 in SHA256SUMS, so
all of them are judged on the same files: tests/zip_consistency.rs holds these copies to those
digests. They are pinned by their bytes, not by a commit: no re-pin of the AstraPlugins goldens
(tests/goldens/astraplugins/PIN) touches them.
AstraPlugins licenses testdata/ under GPL-3.0-or-later (its LICENSE); these files keep that
licence. They are test data this crate's tests read, never part of the launcher's MPL-2.0
sources or of anything it builds.
